module

public meta import Lean.Elab.Command
public meta import Lean.DocString
-- One `import all` line per module of this project's libraries and of the library `Phylogenetics`, so that
-- proofs are visible to the dependency traversal (the module system hides them from a plain `import`):
-- generated by scripts/gen_audit.py.
-- IMPORTS --

/-!
# Axiom and dependency audit

Run with `lake env lean scripts/Audit.lean` after `lake build`.

For every numbered result of the papers, this prints the axioms it depends on and the results from
prior work (`src/External/`, and the papers that another paper cites) that it uses, whether proved there or,
in a conditional formalization, assumed as hypotheses of its statement. It then checks every declaration
of the library and the main theorems of `src/MainResults.lean`. The run fails if any of them
depends on an axiom other than Lean's standard `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound` (a
`sorry` shows up as the axiom `sorryAx`). Its table of results is the source of the report's
dependency table.

It also writes the *route* of every numbered result to `.lake/route_deps.tsv`: the other
numbered results that its proof uses, found by following the proof through the library's helper
lemmas and stopping at numbered results, together with the TeX label that the result's docstring
names in backticks. `scripts/route_check.py` compares these routes with the results that the
papers' proofs cite, in `docs/paper_routes.tsv`.

The library's modules are imported with `import all`, which makes the proofs of their theorems
available: the module system does not export them otherwise. The traversal tests membership in a
precomputed set of the library's constants; looking up each constant's module instead
(`Environment.getModuleIdxFor?`) makes the interpreted script take minutes.

To adapt: generate the `import all` lines, fill in the three lists, and set the libraries' root
names in `isLibraryModule`: the papers' libraries, `External`, the results they cite, `Basic`, the
paper-specific definitions, and `Phylogenetics`, the library of general mathematics, a dependency of this
project. The audit reads that library's proofs as well as this project's, so that one run covers every
axiom that a result depends on; the library's own audit is not assumed.
Keep one `import all` line per module of the libraries, each on its own line: a module that is
missing is still imported through the others, but without its proofs, and the audit then misses the
axioms and the routes inside them. CI checks the list (`scripts/gen_audit.py --check`).
-/

open Lean Elab Command

namespace Audit

